---

<Layout>
  <h1>Ferretboard</h1>
  <p>
    Ferretboard is a small games console running on a custom PCB with a rp2040
    chip and 240x240 screen. It's got various different ways of making games for it, including a web based editor based on a micropython sdk (well, actually 2), and a pure golang compile time system.
  </p>
  <p>
    Created for <a href="https://macondo.hackclub.com/?ref=F2RS4">Hack Club Macondo</a> by <a
      href="https://new.louisbourgault.com">Louis Bourgault du Coudray</a>
  </p>
  <p><a href="/thanks">Acknowledgements</a></p>

  
  
  <h2>Hardware and Physical Device (v1)</h2>
  <p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/shorts/Q-nbf0EjklA">Demo on Youtube of finished device</a></p>
  <img src="https://cdn.hackclub.com/019ee35f-67a7-7709-b699-a4260c96196b/PXL_20260620_040404639.jpg" alt="Photo of the physical device, showing the screen and buttons" />
</Layout>

<style>
  .game-instructions {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  img {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 400px;
  }
</style>